      + `src/` + `include/` + `bindings/wasm/build.sh` (Emscripten C++ build).

(d) **JS wrapper relink mechanism**:
    Users who wish to modify the JS wrapper layer may do so:
    1. Edit `wikey-core/vendor/kiwi-nlp/src/*.ts` as needed.
    2. Build with the upstream `bindings/wasm/build.sh` + Emscripten toolchain
       to regenerate `src/build/kiwi-wasm.{js,d.ts}` (the Emscripten output
       that the TS wrapper imports). The vendor's `dist/` directory is a
       byte-equal mirror of the published npm package's `dist/`; running
       `npm run build` inside the vendor without the upstream Emscripten
       prerequisite will fail with TS2307 (missing `src/build/kiwi-wasm.js`).
       This is intentional — the vendor preserves the JS wrapper TS source
       for inspection/modification, while the prebuilt `dist/` is a working
       copy mirrored from the upstream npm release.
    3. After regenerating `vendor/kiwi-nlp/dist/`, rebuild wikey-obsidian
       with `npm run build` so the plugin re-bundles `main.js` and copies
       `kiwi-wasm.wasm` into the plugin folder root.

(e) **WASM binary relink mechanism (LGPL §6 (d))**:
    Users who wish to modify the WASM binary (Kiwi C++ core) may do so by
    cloning `bab2min/Kiwi` upstream, editing the C++ source, running the
    upstream Emscripten build (`cd bindings/wasm && ./build.sh`), and
    replacing `wikey-core/vendor/kiwi-nlp/dist/kiwi-wasm.wasm` with the
    regenerated artifact. Then rebuild wikey-obsidian.

(f) **Repository public access**: This product's source code is publicly
    available so users can exercise the modification rights granted by
    LGPL §6. The Kiwi dictionary cache at
    `~/.cache/wikey/kiwi-models/cong/base/` (downloaded from upstream Kiwi
    releases) is dictionary data only, separate from the LGPL relink
    mechanism above.

